","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pat-Flfl Rib, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the weight percentage to a weight fraction**:  
   The 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 milliliters of the solution.  
   \[
   \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.00044 \text{ g/mL}
   \]

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL**:  
   \[
   0.00044 \text{ g/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]

3. **Convert grams to milligrams**:  
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

