ΔH°_f_H2O(l) = -285.8 kJ/mol
ΔH°_f_Ca(OH)2(s) = -986.2 kJ/mol

Now, we can calculate the standard enthalpy change:

ΔH = (ΔH°_f_Ca(OH)2(s)) - (ΔH°_f_CaO(s) + ΔH°_f_H2O(l))
ΔH = (-986.2 kJ/mol) - (-635.1 kJ/mol + (-285.8 kJ/mol))
ΔH = (-986.2 kJ/mol) - (-980.9 kJ/mol)
ΔH = -986.2 kJ/mol + 980.9 kJ/mol
