","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{H}_2\text{O}_2 \), in an acidified aqueous solution, the following reactions occur:

1. **Cu^{2+} with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \):**
   \[
   \text{Ca}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \rightarrow \text{CuSO}_3 + \text{H}_2\text{O}
   \]
   The formation of \( \text{Cr}_2\text{O}_3 \) is favored at low concentrations of \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \).

2. **Mn^{2+} with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \):**
   \[
   \text{Mn}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \rightleftharpoons \text{MgCl}_3 + \text{H}_2\text{O}
   \]
   The formation of \( \text{Cr}_2\text{O}_3 \) is favored at low concentrations of \( \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \).

3. **Ni^{2+} with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \):**
   \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \) does not form a complex with \( \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3} \).

4. **Hg^{2+} with \( \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \):**
   \[
   \text{Hg}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \rightleftharpoons \text{MgCl}_{3-} + \text{H}_2\text{O}
   \]

The stability constants for the complexes are:
- \( \text{Cr}_2\text{O}_3: 1.5 \times 10^{-10} \)
- \( \text{MgCl}_{3-}: 1.0 \times 10^{-10} \)

Since \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \) forms a complex with \( \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3 \) with a lower stability constant, it will precipitate preferentially. The other metals form complexes with \( \text{H}_2\text{SO}_3} \) with higher stability constants, so they will not precipitate.

Thus, only \( \text{Cu}_2\text{SO}_3 \) precipitates.

Final Answer: \(\text{Cu}_2\text{SO}_3\)",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
