The optimal ratio of titanium dioxide nanoparticles (TiO2) and graphene oxide (GO) in a composite material for high-performance dye-sensitized solar cells (DSSCs) depends on the specific application and desired properties of the solar cell. However, research has shown that incorporating a certain amount of graphene oxide into the TiO2 matrix can improve the overall efficiency and stability of the solar cell.

