3. $f(x-1) > f(3-2x)$

Since $f(x)$ is increasing on $[0, \infty]$, the inequality $f(x-1) > f(3-2x)$ implies that $x-1 > 3-2x$ for $x-1 \geq 0$ and $3-2x \geq 0$.

