   \[
   \text{Area of each paving slab} = \frac{\text{Total area}}{\text{Number of paving slabs}} = \frac{812.5}{165} = 4.93 \text{ m}^2
   \]

3. **Use the area of the paving slab to find its width**:  
   \[
   \text{Area of paving slab} = \text{Width} \times \text{Width} = 2.25 \times \text{width} = 4.93
