","To calculate the average radiation dose to the liver, we need to use the formula:

\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \0.01 \times \frac{\text{absorbed dose (mSv)}}{\text{mass (g)}}
\]

Given:
- Absorbed dose = 0.12 J
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg = 1,600 g

First, we need to convert the absorbed dose from joules (J) to millisieverts (mSv). The conversion factor is 1 J = 0.01 mSv.

\[
\text{Absained dose (mSv)} = 0.12 \text{ J} \times 10^{-6} \text{ J/mSv} = 1.2 \times 10^{-4} \text{ mSv}
\]

Now, we can use the formula to calculate the dose:

\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \frac{1.2 \times 10^{-4} \text{ mSv}}{1,600 \text{ g}} = 7.5 \times 10^{-5} \text{ mSv/g}
\]

Thus, the average radiation dose to the liver is \(\boxed{7.5 \times 10^{-5} \text{ mSv/g}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
