Thus, the coefficient of intrinsic magnetization \( \kappa_1 \) of the first material increases when it is surrounded by another material with a coefficient of intrinsic magnetization \( \kappa' \). The increase is proportional to \( \kappa' \) and inversely proportional to \( \kappa_1^0 \). 

