<USER_REQUEST>
In a process where hands are rubbed together, the friction force is \( F_{\text{fr}} \) and the mean relative velocity of one hand with respect to the other is \( v \). The room temperature is \( T \). Determine the entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) of this process.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The entropy production rate \( \pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{1}{T} \cdot \text{Power Dissipation} = \frac{1}{T} \cdot \text{Power due to Friction}
\]
The power dissipated by friction is the product of the friction force and the velocity:
\[
\text{Power Dissipation} = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{1}{T} \cdot F_{\text{fr}} v = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
\]
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

