v = 0.6c

Now, we can plug in the values into the time dilation formula:

3 years = t / sqrt(1 - (0.6c)^2/c^2)

3 years = t / sqrt(1 - 0.36)

3 years = t / sqrt(0.64)

3 years = t / 0.8

